ROOT CAUSE VERIFICATION:

From M21-T2-q2-stream.txt:
- Line 159: read step STARTED with URL: https://agaicpower.com/blogs/news/are-home-batteries-safe-lifepo4-vs-nmc-fire-risk-the-real-data-1 (with "-1")
- Line 169 (before fix): read step DONE with URL: https://agaicpower.com/blogs/news/are-home-batteries-safe-lifepo4-vs-nmc-fire-risk-the-real-data-1 (with "-1")
- Line 223: sources event lists URL WITHOUT "-1": https://agaicpower.com/blogs/news/are-home-batteries-safe-lifepo4-vs-nmc-fire-risk-the-real-data

FIX VERIFICATION:

server/src/web/tools.ts:
- Line 188 (before): events.push({ type: "step", data: { step_id, kind: "read", status: "done", url } });
- Line 191 (after): events.push({ type: "step", data: { step_id, kind: "read", status: "done", url: finalUrl } });

The fix changes the done event to use `finalUrl` (which comes from the search service's final_url field at line 187) instead of the requested `url` parameter.

How sources.url gets saved:
server/src/generations/research.ts line 680 extracts source data from source events:
  sources.push({ title: e.data.title, url: e.data.url, n: e.data.n });

The source event comes from tools.ts line 189 which already uses finalUrl:
  events.push({ type: "source", data: n === undefined ? { title, url: finalUrl } : { title, url: finalUrl, n } });

So after the fix, both the done step and the source event use the same finalUrl, ensuring they match.

